@startuml ehds-operating-model
' Rendered by scripts/render-plantuml.sh into docs/security/img/.
title EHDS operating model, secondary use: from onboarding to published results\nResponsibilities by role, Regulation (EU) 2025/327 (adopted numbering)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #64748B
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #D97706
skinparam ActivityStartColor #059669
skinparam ActivityEndColor #059669
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontStyle bold
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #94A3B8

|#F0FDF4|Natural person|
|#EEF2FF|Health data holder|
start
:Registers, proves its identity with a
verifiable credential (DCP, did:web);
|#F8FAFC|Operating company (platform operator)|
:Validates the entity against the national
register, issues the credential;
:Provisions the holder's connector,
keys in the holder's own Vault namespace;
|Health data holder|
:Describes the dataset (Art. 77)
and applies the quality label (Art. 78);
|Operating company (platform operator)|
:Publishes the description in the national
catalogue (HealthDCAT-AP), federates it;
|#FDF2F8|Health data user|
:Discovers the dataset in the catalogue;
:Submits the access application (Art. 67):
purpose, data, safeguards, duration;
|#FFF7ED|Health data access body|
:Checks the application: purpose in Art. 53,
not prohibited by Art. 54, applicant verified;
if (Anonymised data answer the question? (Art. 66)) then (yes)
  :Decides on a data request (Art. 69):
  anonymised statistics only;
else (no)
  :Decides on a permit for
  pseudonymised data (Art. 68);
endif
if (Granted? (decision within three months)) then (no)
  :Refuses with reasons,
  right to complain (Art. 81);
  stop
else (yes)
  :Issues the permit: datasets, purpose,
  conditions, duration, fee (Art. 62);
  :Records it in the public register
  of permits (Art. 58);
endif
|Natural person|
:Is informed about secondary use (Art. 58);
if (Objects?) then (yes)
  :Records the opt-out (Art. 71);
else (no)
endif
|Operating company (platform operator)|
:Evaluates the ODRL policy and the opt-out
register before every extraction;
|Health data holder|
:Extracts the permitted data, pseudonymised,
within the deadline (Art. 60);
:Transfers it through its connector:
DSP contract, data plane;
|Operating company (platform operator)|
:Writes the audit trail: contract, transfer,
every later access (ADR-045);
|#ECFEFF|SPE operator|
:Provides the isolated workspace (Art. 73): no
download, no internet egress, authorised persons only;
repeat
  |Health data user|
  :Works inside the secure processing
  environment on the permitted data only;
  :Requests the release of the results;
  |SPE operator|
  :Logs every access and every output (Art. 73);
  :Checks the output technically:
  cell sizes, direct identifiers;
  |Health data access body|
repeat while (Output free of personal data?) is (no, back to the user) not (yes)
:Releases the results;
|Health data user|
:Publishes the results, naming the
permit and the datasets (Art. 61);
|Health data access body|
:Reports annually (Art. 59),
enforces on misuse (Art. 63);
|SPE operator|
:Is audited at least yearly,
corrective action (Art. 73(3));
stop

legend right
  Controllership: the access body for the secure processing
  environment and the permit data (Art. 74), the holder for its
  source data; the operating company is a processor (GDPR Art. 28).
  The person's opt-out reaches extraction through the operator's
  policy evaluation. No output leaves the SPE without the access body.
endlegend
@enduml
